        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "For reference, I could solve the problem by enabling mini.trailspace only after a new buffer is created:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n    config = function(_, opts)\r\n      require(\"mini.trailspace\").setup(opts)\r\n\r\n      -- HACK: We need to disabel the mini.trailspace and enable when a new buffer is\r\n      -- created to avoid interference with the dashboard snacks.nvim. See:\r\n      --\r\n      --  https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1395\r\n      vim.g.minitrailspace_disable = true\r\n\r\n      vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"BufNew\", {\r\n        callback = function()\r\n          vim.g.minitrailspace_disable = false\r\n        end\r\n      })\r\n  end\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt is probably not the best solution, but it works.",
            "created_at": "2024-12-12T18:02:07Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1395#issuecomment-2539677994",
