        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> This was my very first attempt, but, for some reason, the autocmd was not triggered. I think it has to be something related to the vim initialization that I do not fully understand.\r\n\r\nDo you lazy load 'mini.trailspace', by any chance? In that case its config might be not executing before dashboard is opened. Try moving the `FileType` autocommand inside config for 'snacks.dashboard', as it doesn't require available 'mini.trailspace'.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nAlternatively, there seems to be a 'SnacksDashboardOpened' event. Maybe something like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal f = function(args) vim.b[args.buf].minitrailspace_disable = true end\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', { pattern = 'SnacksDashboardOpened', callback = f })\r\n```\r\n",
            "created_at": "2024-12-12T18:16:40Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1395#issuecomment-2539709385",
