        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "\n> I have both mini and snacks set to `lazy=false`. mini has priority `9999` and snacks has priority `999`.\n> ...\n> Am I missing something? I still see trailspace flashing before its disabled.\n\nSorry, I am not proficient with setting up 'lazy.nvim'. Here is the config that works without flashing using 'mini.nvim' and 'mini.deps':\n\n```lua\nlocal path_package = vim.fn.stdpath('data') .. '/site/'\nlocal mini_path = path_package .. 'pack/deps/start/mini.nvim'\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(mini_path) then\n  vim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\n  local clone_cmd = { 'git', 'clone', '--filter=blob:none', 'https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim', mini_path }\n  vim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\n  vim.cmd('packadd mini.nvim | helptags ALL')\n  vim.cmd('echo \"Installed `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\nend\n\n-- Make sure 'mini.nvim' is available\nvim.cmd(\"packadd mini.nvim\")\n\nrequire(\"mini.deps\").setup()\n\nrequire(\"mini.trailspace\").setup()\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"User\", {\n\tpattern = \"SnacksDashboardOpened\",\n\tcallback = function(args)\n\t\tvim.b[args.buf].minitrailspace_disable = true\n\tend,\n})\n\nMiniDeps.add(\"folke/snacks.nvim\")\nrequire(\"snacks\").setup({\n\tdashboard = {\n\t\tenable = true,\n\t\tsections = {\n\t\t\t{ section = \"header\" },\n\t\t\t{ section = \"keys\", gap = 1, padding = 1 },\n\t\t},\n\t},\n})\n```\n",
